<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item>4.1.1: Contrasting Two Relationships by Reasoning</item>
  <item>4.1.2: Reasoning Graphically About the Relationship between the Two Quantities<list>
      <item>4.1.2: Self Check</item>
      <item>4.1.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>4.1.3 Examining Relations and Functions<list>
      <item>4.1.3: Self Check</item>
      <item>4.1.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>4.1.4: Describing Functional Relationships<list>
      <item>4.1.4: Self Check</item>
      <item>4.1.4: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>4.1.5: Modeling Relationships between Two Variables</item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 4.1.6: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list>
  <item>Graphing technology</item>
  <item><link title="handout" url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/92f802ec9f83af78671273f5a9e7e05acb8dfe92">4.1.2 Activity Graphing Printable</link></item>
  <item>Coordinate grids</item>
</list>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<para>Make copies of coordinate grids and the 4.1.2 graphing activity printable.</para>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look for
    these words and notice their use and meanings.</item>
  <item>Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral explanations.
  </item>
  <item>Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link></item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
